@startuml
title applyPotentiallyNewLocalItem()
start

note right
  Input has already passed online filtering / scope checks
  and the online item is not currently tracked as this identity.

  "New" here means new to the database identity map. A local
  pathname can already exist, so this path must not assume that
  it is safe to overwrite whatever is on disk.
end note

if (Target path already exists locally?) then (yes)
  if (Invalid symbolic link?) then (yes)
    :Skip item;
    stop
  endif

  :Call isItemSynced() using online item metadata;
  if (Reported in sync?) then (yes)
    if (File-like item has no trusted DB identity\nand content hash differs?) then (yes)
      :Do not bind equal-timestamp but different content;
      :Continue conflict reconciliation;
      note right
        Equal timestamps alone are not enough to prove
        that an untracked local file is the same content.
        This prevents the client from binding the wrong
        local bytes to an online DriveItem identity.
      end note
    else (no)
      :Upsert online identity / metadata into DB;
      if (Remote/shared item?) then (yes)
        :Create / update required shared-folder DB tie records;
      endif
      if (write_xattr_data enabled?) then (yes)
        :Write OneDrive metadata to xattr;
      endif
      stop
    endif
  endif

  :Compare local and online modification timestamps\nat whole-second resolution;
  if (Local timestamp is newer?) then (yes)
    if (Online identity already exists in DB?) then (yes)
      :Keep local file;\nno replacement queued;
      stop
    else (no)
      if (Local content already matches online hash?) then (yes)
        :Correct local timestamp to authoritative online timestamp;
        :Upsert online item in DB;
        stop
      else (no)
        :Content differs; replacement decision is deferred\nto transactional download commit;
        note right
          Local data is NOT destroyed here. If online content
          must ultimately replace this pathname, the download
          commit boundary re-evaluates the canonical file and
          creates safeBackup when preservation is required.
        end note
      endif
    endif
  else (no)
    if (Online timestamp is newer?) then (yes)
      if (Local content matches online hash?) then (yes)
        :Correct local timestamp;
        :Upsert online item in DB;
        stop
      else (no)
        :Different content; queue authoritative online replacement;
        note right
          Replacement is transactional. Unique local content
          is preserved before the staged online file can become
          the canonical local file.
        end note
      endif
    else (timestamps equal)
      if (Content hash matches?) then (yes)
        :Upsert online item in DB;
        stop
      else (no)
        :Equal timestamp does not imply equal content;\nqueue authoritative online replacement;
        note right
          The download transaction owns any later safeBackup
          requirement; this function does not destructively
          rename or overwrite the existing local file.
        end note
      endif
    endif
  endif
else (no)
  :No local object occupies target path;
endif

switch (Online item type)
case (file)
  :Queue file JSON for download;
case (directory)
  :Create local directory and persist metadata;
case (remote directory)
  :Create local shared-folder directory / ties;
case (remote file)
  :Queue file JSON for download;
case (root / unknown / none)
  :No local file action here;
endswitch

stop
@enduml
